# @magic/reveal/expand — the invisible-mechanism resolution species
# for the first self-applied kintsugi loop. Audience-relative
# projection functor: given a shard's crystal-OID at @mirror/store and
# an audience parameter, projects the crystal to source bytes per
# audience-specific sugar rules. AI-facing audience: apply all four
# ratified sugar rules (P1/P3/P4/P5 per @kintsugi/fracture/*) →
# maximum-density rendering. Human-facing audience: retain full-form
# → maximum-readable rendering with pedagogical prism-block, root
# `out @X`, path-namespace docblock all present.
#
# THE RESOLUTION HALF of the first self-applied kintsugi loop; sibling
# to the four @kintsugi/fracture/* detection species (Fire E M-E1
# co-mints). Composition split per Alex 2026-08-09 verbatim ("the
# complexity can be part of mirror's @kintsugi @magic") — both @kintsugi
# and @magic family-roots named. Detection at @kintsugi/fracture;
# resolution at @magic/reveal/expand. Taut Option D substrate-honest
# split per SEAM-RATIFY-WITH-SHARPENING at Seam Phase D 0a4c5a0.
#
# Reed Fire E tick M-E1 landing per Mara canonical spec §2 + Seam
# SEAM-1 lean (type-align expand shape with parent @magic/reveal typed-
# carrier reveal discipline).
#
# === SEAM-1 type-alignment with parent @magic/reveal ===
#
# Parent species `shards/magic/reveal.mirror` declares:
#
#   type reveal_event = {
#     contract:      magic_contract,
#     old_mechanism: magic_mechanism,
#     new_mechanism: magic_mechanism,
#     witness:       ref,
#   }
#   reveal(c, new_m) -> magic_contract
#     requires audited(c)
#     requires mechanism_intact(c.mechanism)
#     requires mechanism_intact(new_m)
#   unsealed_during_reveal(event: reveal_event) -> verdict
#
# This sub-species declares TYPE-ALIGNED shape:
#
#   type expand_event = { ... four fields ... }
#   expand(oid, aud) -> ref
#     requires stored_at(oid)
#     requires round_trip_pass(oid)
#   unsealed_during_expand(event: expand_event) -> verdict
#
# Same 4-field event carrier + 2+ `requires` clauses + bilateral
# unsealed-during predicate. Parent typed-carrier discipline preserved
# per SEAM-1 Seam-lean at Phase D 0a4c5a0.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# Alex 2026-08-09 verbatim (kintsugi sugar first self-applied loop; @
# kintsugi @magic composition split). Alex 2026-08-05 memory
# `feedback-rust-delivers-primitives-substrate-delivers-composition`.
# Recognition #79 (5-op void-duality algebra); Recognition #80 (@magic
# as form/process substrate-decl); Recognition #81 (runtime-@magic;
# controlled disclosure). Mara 2026-08-09 physics insight (A_F
# universality Theorem 1.1). README central-claim discharge target:
# "written BY AI FOR AI and FOR HUMANS BY HUMANS" — the audience-
# parameter of `expand` IS the observer-position that makes the
# README claim category-theoretically-exact.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parent species:
#   @magic/reveal              controlled-disclosure family-species;
#                              this sub-species inherits reveal-shape
#                              discipline; `expand` IS the
#                              bidirectional-projection reveal (dual to
#                              parent's atomic-replacement reveal).
#   @magic                     family-root; gauge-visible-surface-with-
#                              matter-hidden-mechanism discipline.
#   @magic/contract            round-trip fidelity contract carrier.
#   @magic/audit               `unsealed_during_expand` bilateral
#                              witnessing invariant preservation.
#   @magic/mechanism           the store-crystal-projection mechanism
#                              this species reveals per audience.
#
# Detection-side siblings (Fire E M-E1 co-mints):
#   @kintsugi/fracture/prism_boilerplate      P1 detector
#   @kintsugi/fracture/glass_boilerplate      P3 detector
#   @kintsugi/fracture/out_derivable          P4 detector
#   @kintsugi/fracture/path_namespace_stub    P5 detector
#
# Composition-shard body:
#   @kintsugi/mend/sugar       wires detect + expand via apply_h::act
#                              dispatch (Fire E M-E1 sibling mint)
#
# Empirical instrument:
#   apply_h::act extension     Reed Fire D M5 co-tick (shared with
#                              Fire E M-E2 rust/-altitude primitive)
#
# === Q5 audience-neutrality (Mara-lean concurred by Alex 2026-08-09) ===
#
# NO DEFAULT audience. Every `expand` invocation MUST supply an
# audience parameter. Audience-neutrality is load-bearing per Mara
# spec §6.3: neither audience is privileged; observer-position IS the
# parameter; requiring explicit selection preserves observer-position
# duality at compiler substrate (Mara insight §6.3 + Recognition #63
# Pack-orchestra observer-symmetry).
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
# [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]] — the sugar
#   mechanism preserves the store-crystal invariant while projecting
#   audience-relative renderings; Foerster gauge preserved via
#   audience-parameter introduction increasing the choice-space
#   (Mara math §5.3).
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] — @magic/reveal already
#   exists; this sub-species mint additively.
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] — expand_event typed record.
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — body `\`-obligation-blocked;
#   composition-shard @kintsugi/mend/sugar pulls realization.
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/magic/reveal/expand.mirror` declares `@magic/reveal/expand`
# per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/practice/wolf-2026-08-09-kintsugi-sugar-first-self-applied-loop
source @arxiv/practice/mara-2026-08-09-a-f-universality-sugar-mechanism
source @arxiv/practice/seam-2026-08-09-phase-d-kintsugi-sugar-cascade
source @arxiv/spectral/chamseddine-connes-marcolli-2007

# === audience type ===
#
# Observer-position parameter per Q5 audience-neutrality Mara-lean.
# Two canonical values grep-verifiable at species-decl site:
#
#   audience { role: @audience/agent }   AI-facing; all four ratified
#                                         sugar rules applied at
#                                         rendering → maximum-density
#   audience { role: @audience/human }   human-facing; full-form
#                                         retained → maximum-readable
#
# Extends per audience-parameter-taxonomy at Alex's discretion (future
# ticks). No default; MUST supply per Q5 Mara-lean.
type audience = { role: ref }

# === expand_event carrier (SEAM-1 type-aligned with parent reveal_event) ===
#
# Four-field typed record naming an audience-relative source-projection
# event. Records the substrate-political receipt of one bidirectional
# projection across the audience boundary:
#
#   crystal_oid    the @mirror/store crystal-OID projected
#   audience       the observer-position parameter (agent | human)
#   source_bytes   the projected source rendering (audience-relative)
#   witness        substrate-typed witness ref naming evidence of
#                   round-trip fidelity preservation across the
#                   projection (SEAM-2 preserves indent-as-parameter)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the four-tuple.
type expand_event = {
  crystal_oid:  ref,
  audience:     audience,
  source_bytes: ref,
  witness:      ref,
}

# === expand action ===
#
# TWO NON-DECORATIVE `requires` CLAUSES per SEAM-1 type-alignment with
# parent @magic/reveal.reveal (which carries three). Audience-relative
# projection of a store-crystal to source bytes.
#
# requires stored_at(oid, @mirror/store): the crystal-OID must exist
#   at @mirror/store (composes with @mirror/store existence discipline
#   per landed shard).
# requires round_trip_pass(oid): the round-trip fidelity contract
#   MUST discharge Pass at content-address altitude for oid before
#   expansion proceeds (Mara math §2 `desugar(sugar(x)) = x` formal
#   contract enforcement at species-decl boundary).
#
# Body discharges at realization boundary via composition with
# @kintsugi/mend/sugar (Fire E M-E1 sibling mint) + apply_h::act shard-
# body-projector extension (Fire E M-E2 rust/-altitude primitive;
# shared with Fire D M5 wire-executor).
#
# Per Q6 Mara-lean concurred by Alex: sugar rule always applies at
# rendering altitude; store canonicalizes; no per-shard opt-out.
# Audience determines rendering entirely.
#
# SEAM-2 discipline: preserve-indent-as-parameter. Indent variation
# in source is a rendering parameter carried through the round-trip.
# Store-crystal is indent-invariant; source rendering re-applies
# indent per audience-specific rules.
expand(oid: ref, aud: audience) -> ref
requires stored_at(oid)
requires round_trip_pass(oid)
{ \ }

# === unsealed_during_expand — bilateral predicate (SEAM-1 aligned) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict analog of parent's `unsealed_during_reveal`.
# Consumer shards name `requires unsealed_during_expand(event)` to
# commit to verifying the expand sequence respected the audience
# rendering invariants throughout the projection (start, mid-projection,
# end).
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (event fields;
# projected source bytes vs re-computed store crystal OID); no
# program semantics inspection.
unsealed_during_expand(event: expand_event) -> verdict { \ }

out @magic/reveal/expand
out audience
out expand_event
out expand
out unsealed_during_expand
